{
  "bio_short": "NAOBA is the sound of Tamara Montenegro, a Nicaraguan-German producer, DJ and sound artist amplifying consciousness through music. Her music works like architecture made of frequency. Sub-bass pulses, ancestral rhythm and fine organic textures lock into geometric patterns, like sand drawing sacred shapes on a vibrating plate, her sound is very much for the body as much as as to take pleasure in listening. \n\nThe dance floor becomes ritual as she is a dancer herself. The studio, a laboratory where psychoacoustics, codes and intuition meet. Each set is a journey that guides deep somatic experiences, soothing or activating the nervous system and returning listeners and dancers to a remembrance. \n\nHer music was in consideration for the Latin Grammy 2026, her scores accompany films honoured at Diversity in Cannes, and her work has been presented at ISEA Dubai, Sound Art Festival Mexico City and TEDx.",
